# Regions excluded from ichorCNA binning, beyond centromeres.
#
# ichorCNA's shipped centromere_acen file covers centromeres and acrocentric
# arms only. Bins outside those regions can still carry corrected log2 values
# no copy state can produce - depth ratios of one in hundreds or thousands -
# because they are mapping failures rather than copy-number events: the MHC,
# where hg38 carries alt haplotypes; subtelomeres; and known blacklist
# intervals.
#
# The effect is not subtle when it occurs. A handful of such bins can carry
# essentially all the genome-wide variance, and the HMM cannot fit any tumour
# fraction that accommodates them, so every chromosome is smoothed into a
# single neutral segment and a real arm-level event is reported as neutral at
# tumour fraction 0.
#
# PROVENANCE. These intervals were identified on the acute-leukaemia cohort in
# the sibling pipeline, not on this one. They are properties of the hg38
# assembly rather than of any disease or cohort, which is why they carry over,
# but the list has not been verified against this project's samples. Treat it
# as a starting point and confirm it before relying on the segment calls.
#
# To re-derive from this cohort's own data, rank the 1 Mb bins by corrected
# log2 and inspect the tail:
#
#   awk 'NR>1 && $NF != "NA"' results/hg38/calls/ichorcna/*/*.cna.seg \
#     | sort -k5,5g | head -40
#
# A bin whose corrected log2 sits below about -1.0 while the interquartile
# range of the genome is a few hundredths is not a deletion. Add it here, or
# remove an interval below that this cohort does not reproduce.
#
# Concatenated with the centromere file and the panel BED in
# modules/local/ichorcna.nf. Coordinates are hg38, chr-prefixed to match.
#
# Ploidy estimation is deliberately left enabled in this pipeline. Fixing
# ploidy at 2 is correct for a disease whose genome is near-diploid, but
# hyperdiploidy is a defining event in myeloma and constraining the fit would
# discard it. Masking these bins is what stabilises the fit here, not
# narrowing the ploidy search.
#
# Chr	Start	End
chr6	28000000	34000000
chr15	28000000	32000000
chr8	1	2000000
chr17	1	2000000
chr1	244000000	246000000
chr4	67000000	69000000
chr6	127000000	129000000
chr8	38000000	40000000
